              "suggestedAnswer": "Answer Outline:\n1. **Definition**: Plastic fragments under 5mm arising from textile degradation, industrial wear, or physical weathering of trash.\n2. **Marine Hazard**: Plankton misidentify microplastics as food, leading to trophic transfers (bioaccumulation) up the marine web to top fish predators, translating to toxic dietary ingestion risks in humans.\n3. **Regulatory Cures**: Expanding Extended Producer Responsibility (EPR), enforcing filters in commercial laundry hubs, and international maritime plastic pacts.\n4. **Conclusion**: Safeguarding blue economy assets requires integrated coastal waste-routing strategies."
