              "suggestedAnswer": "Answer Outline:\n1. **Natural Fragility**: Situated on old glacial landslide material in the seismic Zone V of fragile Himalayan slopes.\n2. **Anthropogenic Triggers**: Unregulated multi-story hotel buildings exceeding geographic load capacity, high blasting for bypass highways, and lack of systematic sewage systems leading to soil lubrication.\n3. **Way Forward**: Strict physical carrying capacity reviews, bio-engineering slope stabilization, and absolute freeze on heavy infrastructural projects in hazard-sensitive micro-zones.\n4. **Conclusion**: Balancing hill development demands structural containment and eco-centric planning."
