              "id": "q1_2015_g1",
              "num": "1(a)",
              "text": "Examine the role of the Governor as a constitutional head and an agent of the Central Government. Discuss the friction areas.",
              "marks": 5,
              "suggestedAnswer": "Answer Outline:\n1. **Constitutional Role**: Article 153-154 provides for a Governor as the executive head who usually acts on aid and advice under Article 163.\n2. **Agent Capacity**: Acts as a dynamic link between federal Center and States, transmitting reports under situations like Article 356.\n3. **Friction Areas**: Delays/withholding assent to bills passed by elective legislatures (Article 200), choosing CMs in hung houses, and political biases in recommending President's Rule.\n4. **Conclusion**: Aligning Governor conducts with Sarkaria/Punchhi commissions is critical to preserving robust federal balance."
