              "suggestedAnswer": "Answer Outline:\n1. **Concept**: Transitions from linear resource flows (‘take-make-discard’) to circular designs targeting recycling, upcycling, and extending materials value.\n2. **Relevance**: India generates massive municipal waste, mostly dumped unprocessed in landfills, causing ecological stress.\n3. **Applications**: Compulsory organic composting, waste-to-energy transformations, and Extended Producer Responsibility (EPR) on plastics.\n4. **Conclusion**: Circular models reduce raw resource strains and foster green business innovations, advancing Swachh Bharat 2.0 goals."
