              "suggestedAnswer": "The decline of the Indus Valley (Harappan) Civilization was multi-causal rather than sudden. Key theories include:\n1. **Ecological and Climatic Changes:** Weakening of the monsoons and subsequent drying of the Ghaggar-Hakra (Saraswati) river system severely impacted agriculture.\n2. **Tectonic Shifts and Floods:** Tectonic disturbances altered river courses, leading to either devastating floods or acute water scarcity.\n3. **Decline in Trade:** Collapse of long-distance trade with Mesopotamia weakened the urban economic base.\n4. **Over-exploitation of Resources:** Deforestation for baking bricks led to soil erosion.\n5. **Aryan Invasion/Internal Discord:** Though disputed, early historians suggested external invasions; contemporary consensus leans toward gradual migration and ruralization."
