              "suggestedAnswer": "India's low and historically declining Female Labor Force Participation Rate (FLFPR) is driven by multiple structural factors:\n1. **Income Effect:** As household incomes rise, women often withdraw from manual labor to manage households, which carries higher social status in conservative communities.\n2. **Educational Enrollment:** More young women are pursuing higher education, delaying their entry into the workforce.\n3. **Lack of Safe/Suitable Jobs:** A deficit of secure, flexible, and formal jobs near rural/semi-urban areas, coupled with safety concerns during commutes.\n4. **Domestic and Care Burden:** The disproportionate burden of unpaid domestic and care work.\n5. **Agrarian Mechanization:** Mechanization of agriculture has displaced manual female labor without matching opportunities in manufacturing."
